<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the SellerWidget extension target.

  The App Group is the ONLY storage an app and its widget extension can share —
  separate processes, separate sandboxes — so without this entry the widget can
  never see the payload `SellerWidgetService` writes, and renders its empty state
  forever with no error anywhere.

  ⚠️ This must match, character for character:

    * `kAppGroupId` in SellerWidget.swift
    * `SellerWidgetService.iOSAppGroupId` in lib/services/seller_widget_service.dart
    * the same key in the RUNNER target's entitlements (the app is the writer)

  The Runner half is NOT included here because `Runner/Runner.entitlements`
  already exists for Universal Links and is itself not yet wired into the Xcode
  project (see the note in that file). Both halves are added in Xcode — see
  ios/README_SELLER_WIDGET.md.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.solevision.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
